WEBVTT

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.360
What are you trying to say?

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.350
Exactly what it sounds like.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.870
You should let me handle it.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.400
Handle it?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.570
They're poorly formed.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.810
I want to display my skill as a chef

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.180
by testing myself with 
such rough ingredients.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.080
Explain it to me 
so I can understand.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.460
I'm saying with my skills,

00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:00.140
I can turn any potato into a dish 
worthy of a three-star restaurant.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:01.640
What?

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.390
Sheesh.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.060
Music producer Hayasaka Tasuku.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.150
Isn't the I-1 Club 
one of your clients?

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.270
No one can constrain me.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.790
Besides...

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:22.780
The I-1 Club doesn't 
inspire me anymore.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.290
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:35.050
<b>Composer Hayasaka Tasuku</b>

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.410
Today, we'd like 
to welcome to the studio

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:35.050
the man responsible for the I-1 Club's 
sudden success and now known

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.070
throughout the world as a genius 
producer, Hayasaka Tasuku-san.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.680
Thank you.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:49.540
<b>Composer Hayasaka Tasuku</b>

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.070
We heard you recently 
have been receiving work

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.490
not only from the I-1 Club 
but also from abroad.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.560
How do you feel about that?

00:02:49.540 --> 00:03:02.320
<b>Composer Hayasaka Tasuku</b>

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.250
I don't know how to answer that.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:56.010
I don't care if the work 
is domestic or international.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.940
Besides, my work isn't about money.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.320
It's about passion.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.410
Not about money?

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.700
<b>Goal: Sendai 
Primetime!!</b>

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.700
That's what rich people say.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.050
President, look at this.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:17.320
This Hayasaka guy's an obvious 
nouveau riche and unlikeable guy...

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.890
The rainy season has 
finally come to Sendai.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:33.350
<b>Tomorrow</b>

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.640
Things are about to get 
really, really wet.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.330
Try to stay dry.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:31.300
It may be dry and sunny right now, 
but it should rain tonight.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.350
Don't forget your portable umbrella.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.290
Good evening!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:38.360
It's time for "Sorry It's So Short" 
with Wake Up, Girls!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.990
Recently, I've been really 
into impersonations.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.210
I'd like to perform a few for you.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.870
First up is my school's PE teacher.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.120
Is that true?

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.380
Why would I lie?

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.490
We're going to write this down, 
so we can't fight about it later.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.240
Matsuda!

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.010
Yes!

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:08.760
I don't mind signing something, 
but why are you so suspicious?

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.470
Because not only will you 
give us a ton of money,

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.680
but you don't want any in return.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.270
It's far too suspicious.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.780
I told you that I don't want money.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.400
Then, what <i>do</i> you want?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.810
I just want to cook some dirty

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:29.660
and rough potatoes 
that can capture my interest.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.160
You'll understand eventually.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:37.300
When I return to Sendai next week,

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.170
I'll be taking those little potatoes.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.420
Sure. That's fine.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.930
See you later, then.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.660
There's one thing I want to make clear.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.800
What might that be?

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.330
Does I-1 know about this?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.310
I haven't told them anything.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.120
What? You haven't asked 
for their permission?

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.590
Why should I worry 
about what he thinks?

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:04.320
But...

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.800
Isn't everyone forever 
under I-1's control

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.700
because we're constantly 
worried about how he feels?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.840
I think he'd have 
more purpose if someone

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.210
who could catch him 
off guard were to appear.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:19.210
I see...

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:25.440
Besides, he doesn't own me, 
and I'll work with whoever I want.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.470
That's all.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.390
You may be fine with that,

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.010
but we don't want to pick 
pointless fights with I-1.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:33.970
You understand that, don't you?

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:39.970
I'm sure Shiraki-san knows Green 
Leaves can't draw me away from him.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.160
It'll be fine.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.740
After all, I'm the one 
who approached you this time.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.620
Is that all?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.240
See you next week.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:58.710
This is getting crazy, President.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:03.590
Are you shaking?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:04.880
I can't help it!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.890
What a bunch of country bumpkins.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.390
But that's what makes you so great.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.520
First, I'd like to hear 
each one of your voices.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.640
Say, "ah."

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.150
Ah.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.280
That voice.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.410
It sounds just like an idol's.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.340
Throw away everything 
you've been holding onto.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.410
Start from there.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.870
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:38.550
What?!

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:39.870
Hayasaka-san is?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.120
He's going to give us lessons?

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.500
Why so suddenly?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.360
I'd like to know, too.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.820
And he's doing it free of charge.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:47.950
Seriously?

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:50.630
They say there's nothing 
more expensive than free.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.200
You're right.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:55.390
<b>Goal: Sendai 
Primetime!!</b>

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.390
He gave us a few conditions, too.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:56.640
Conditions?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.640
Yes, conditions.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:07.150
<b>Goal: Sendai Primetime!!</b>

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.550
Let's see...

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:04.040
Hayasaka-san will be coming to Sendai

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.150
every Saturday for your lessons.

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.200
You're terrible.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.160
You're not producing 
your voices from your stomach.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.370
Listen up.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:23.670
Improving your physical fitness 
before you get onstage is fundamental.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.190
One hundred more times.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.930
Long lessons every weekend, huh?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.800
We've got school and 
recordings on weekdays,

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.360
so we have hardly any time to rest.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.740
I feel like a celebrity.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.900
You're not <i>like</i> a celebrity, you <i>are</i> one.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.490
Have some more self-awareness.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.790
I don't know if I can keep up.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.820
That's not all.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:51.320
<b>Goal: Sendai 
Primetime!!</b>

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.220
Every second and fourth Saturday,

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.320
you'll perform three 
concerts in one day.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.410
What?!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.370
Next pose.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.340
Okay, next pose.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.590
Next.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:04.370
Okay, now listen like that.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.660
First, as I told you before,

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.840
next Saturday, you'll perform three concerts.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.340
Are you listening?

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.430
We're listening...

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.730
Then respond.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:17.970
Y-Yes!

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:23.400
I saw your performance 
the other day, but honestly, no.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.230
That wasn't enough. 
It was unprofessional.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:30.530
It's not unreasonable, though. 
You don't have much experience.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.580
That's why I've planned for you

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.490
to perform more concerts 
and learn through experience.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.300
Your first concert, well...

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:41.430
You don't have many songs, 
so we'll call it an hour.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:46.560
I was thinking we'd plan for concerts 
at 2 PM, 4 PM, and 6 PM.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.750
Hey, are you listening?

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.600
Yes!

00:08:55.610 --> 00:09:00.330
Um... My legs are exhausted.

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:03.180
Yeah. I should be hungry, 
but I'm so tired,

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.000
I don't have the energy to eat.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.510
What? You lost your appetite?

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:12.270
We're training like this 
again tomorrow, right?

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:13.660
I might die.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:17.050
Yeah. This is harder than 
my job at the gas station.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:20.030
How long do we have to keep 
doing this brutal training?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:27.540
<b>Goal: Sendai 
Primetime!!</b>

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.590
Finally, Hayasaka-san 
will have full power over

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.540
Wake Up, Girls! 
for a period of time.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.790
What does that mean?

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:36.800
<b>Goal: Sendai 
Primetime!!</b>

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:36.800
In other words, we can't complain 
about anything Hayasaka-san does.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.590
What?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:40.820
What should we do?

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.080
Do you want to stop by the agency?

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.560
I want to go home.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.740
I agree.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.360
Me, too.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:53.430
Mayushi, has Hayasaka-san 
always been so strict?

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.070
Huh? Oh.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.210
We weren't there at the same time,

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:59.560
so this is my first time 
experiencing his lessons.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.950
I see.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:06.310
But don't you feel like 
you're really working hard?

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:07.610
You think so?

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.950
I think I'm going to be depressed.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.230
Me, too.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.460
Don't worry about it on your own.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.610
You can talk to us about anything.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.970
We're a group. Let's come 
up with something together.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.970
<b>Senichiya</b>

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.970
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:30.230
Shimada Mayu, Nanase Yoshino, 
Katayama Minami, Hisami Nanami.

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.480
These four are fine.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.080
Then there's Okamoto Miyu 
and Kikuma Kaya.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:37.740
Despite both being amateurs, 
they'll manage somehow.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.240
The bottleneck is Hayashida Airi.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.910
I'm thinking of cutting her.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:44.620
What?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.240
Wait...

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.580
Whoa, there.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.750
You said you wouldn't question me.

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.550
Mayushi's dancing is so on point.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:04.230
Minami is cute, and Yoppi is cool.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.060
Kayatan's kind of sexy, too.

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.520
Miyu seems to know how 
to draw people to her,

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.020
and Nanami has this 
magnificence, too.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.770
Compared to them, what is this?

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:20.140
I need to work harder...

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.120
But I'm so glad to be 
working with everyone!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.870
Airi, time for dinner!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.290
Okay!

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.290
Airi, you haven't had 
any breaks recently.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.040
Are you okay?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.050
Yeah. My lessons are tough.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:40.700
It's kind of fun, though.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.710
You sure you're not dragging 
everyone down with you?

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.050
Maybe.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.590
But everyone has 
their own personality.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.400
Everyone in WUG is so talented.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.560
I think they're so cool.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.510
Then you're just a fan.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.540
I am. I'm a huge fan.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.730
Oh, yeah. You should 
come to one of our concerts.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:07.530
I'd be too embarrassed 
to watch you perform!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.460
We're right in the middle 
of the rainy season.

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.320
It's been raining every day,

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:15.450
I never get the chance 
to hang my laundry.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.960
It's so sad.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:26.470
<b>Tomorrow</b>

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.550
I hate hanging my clothes up indoors.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:23.770
Laundry needs to receive the sun's rays.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:27.010
Tomorrow, it will rain 
first thing in the morning,

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.570
but from afternoon to evening, 
the skies should be clear.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:32.930
Right, Ai-chan?

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.170
Yes?

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:35.500
Oh, um...

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:41.570
Y-Your laundry might get 
some sun if you hang it then.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.380
We're in commercial!

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.950
Thank you very much!

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.220
Uh, um...

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.490
I-I'm so sorry!

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.310
What's wrong?

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.750
Did you let your guard down 
now that you're used to the show?

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.490
I-It's not like that!

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:56.080
I was just spacing out.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.750
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:04.650
You've all been seeming 
a little tired lately.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:05.540
Are you okay?

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.600
You're professionals.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.810
No matter how hard things get, 
you need to bring the energy.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.580
Good work today.

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.590
Thank you.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.220
I'm sorry. It's my fault...

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:19.980
Don't worry about it.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.820
Bring the energy, huh?

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.840
It's not that easy.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.250
With all the energy we've been burning,

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:28.780
we may have unconsciously 
been less energetic.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:32.280
And on days we have three concerts...

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.590
That's all for today.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:39.290
Thank you very much.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.550
Hayashida Airi.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.550
Yes.

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:45.550
You stay.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.800
Y-Yes.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:03.260
Are you waiting for Airi?

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:05.140
Yeah.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.700
It might take a while.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.470
Sorry, but I'm at my limit. 
I want to go home.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:11.990
Me, too.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.270
Can we let our leader 
handle this one?

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:16.450
Huh? Me?

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.960
I'll be fine by myself. You can go.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.330
Thanks for staying.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.830
Thanks.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:33.470
So... Hayashida Airi, why did you 
audition for Wake Up, Girls!?

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:37.470
In fact, why do you want to be an idol?

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:41.430
Um... I guess I wanted to change myself.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.230
That's why I decided to apply.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.980
How do you feel now that you're doing it?

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.640
It's far more fun than I imagined.

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:51.280
Why are you having fun?

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:54.390
Do you not understand what I'm saying?

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.790
Which one are you?

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.750
Which what?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:01.440
We're creators.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.230
We're the ones entertaining the audience.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:07.630
You may be better suited 
to being a member of the audience.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:12.850
Honestly speaking, I don't 
think you have any talent.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.650
If you're going to reconsider, now is the time.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.430
That's all I have to say.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:22.440
Good work today.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:26.220
Th-Thank you!

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:52.720
You waited for me?

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.960
I had everyone else leave.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.920
They seemed to be at their limit.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:58.890
I see.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.050
Let's go home.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.480
I'm starving.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:07.610
Sorry. I'm going to stop 
by the convenience store.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.490
Oh... Okay...

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:26.540
It seems the Sendai 
opening concert ended

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.250
the other day without any problems.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.490
Good work, participating members.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.450
Thanks to you, it was a huge success.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.760
Is what I'd like to say, but...

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:39.090
The tickets were sold out,

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:42.980
but there were three people 
who didn't come that day.

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:45.460
Were they sick?

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:48.790
Were they unable to come because 
their grandfather fell ill?

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:52.240
Did they swallow their tears 
due to work or studies?

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.240
We don't know the reason.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.660
This is the first time 
it's happened during

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.510
the I-1 Club's National 47 Prefecture 
Love Connection Project.

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:03.500
I've analyzed the data myself,

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.500
<b>Home</b>

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.500
<b>Animal Weather Report</b>

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.500
<b>We're Always Right!</b>

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.350
and it seems local idol group

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:09.000
Wake Up, Girls! had a concert on the same day.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.000
<b>Local Gourmet 
Super Delicious</b>

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:09.000
<b>It's really tasty, meow!</b>

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.350
This...

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.260
It's Wake Up, Girls!...

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:17.830
I suppose you could call 
them an unrefined or

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.650
unaffected product of only Sendai.

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:23.020
They're just a little 
countryside idol group.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.570
If you're laughing right now, you're wrong.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:33.400
I suspect they will catch up 
to you in the near future.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.070
When they do, let's break them down!

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:38.070
Yes!

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.320
Yes!

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:42.170
Let us conclude this day by singing

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.330
the necessary attributes 
of a popular idol together.

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:47.210
Don't rest! Don't complain! Don't think!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.210
Don't rest! Don't complain! Don't think!

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:51.990
Always gratitude!

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.340
Always gratitude!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:59.840
Today's your first day 
of back-to-back concerts.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:03.350
Honestly, we have a lot 
of tickets leftover.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.480
It's a fight to see how 
large of an audience

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.350
we can gather for 
the 2 o'clock show.

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:09.880
Doing so will increase the 
number of repeat customers

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:11.360
for the 4 and 6 o'clock shows.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:12.610
Yes, sir!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:15.610
Miyu-chan, you've got us!

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.110
You can do it!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:24.200
<i>Believing I could not dream</i>

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.410
<i>I protected my small, qui—</i>

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.370
You should hammer into your 
brains that this is the best

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:33.420
you can do right now.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.930
You're off key.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.420
You can't dance properly.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:42.930
I'm pretty sure kindergarten plays 
are a little better these days.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.700
Are you frustrated?

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.680
Then show me a performance 
that will even impress me.

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:51.940
If you can't, there's still 
time in a lot of ways.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:58.320
Well, see you next week.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.450
I can't take it anymore.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:05.630
What? You're done eating?

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:08.890
No, not that. I'm talking 
about Hayasaka-san.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:09.710
Oh...

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.710
You know I'm someone 
who grows with praise.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.210
I don't know anything about that.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:21.220
Well, when someone keeps telling 
me I'm bad, I lose all my energy.

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:24.220
Yeah, I might have 
thought about that, too.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.220
What?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.660
Being abused like that 
really pisses me off.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.140
If this were one of my jobs, 
I'd have quit a long time ago.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.230
Yeah...

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:36.230
Like why are we even doing this?

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:48.750
There's still time in a lot of ways.

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:58.800
<b>If you want it, you can do it</b>

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:05.020
Airi, it's time for dinner!

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.920
Airi!

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:10.970
Okay...

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:18.230
<i>People often ask me what a captain does,</i>

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:23.140
<i>and I think I have the strength 
to support my team from the shadows.</i>

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:24.060
<i>For example,</i>

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:25.630
<i>when someone looks like they're about</i>

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.620
<i>to mentally fall from the stage,</i>

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.490
<i>I support them, so they don't fall.</i>

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.810
<i>It can be hard, but because 
it's for the team,</i>

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:34.820
<i>I've never disliked doing it.</i>

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.370
Mayu, where's Airi?

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.850
Huh? She's not here?

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.540
She's usually the first or second one here.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:58.860
She's never been late.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.980
She didn't get in an accident, did she?

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:04.570
Don't be so negative!

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:06.150
This isn't good.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:09.030
He said he wouldn't hold 
lessons if anyone was late.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:09.680
It's no use.

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:10.590
She's not answering.

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:19.570
Um, Airi's still not here.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:22.570
Ai-chan's never been late before.

00:21:22.570 --> 00:21:24.080
We thought something 
might have happened to her.

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:27.740
I did some of my own thinking 
after last week's performance.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:33.390
In my opinion, Wake Up, Girls! 
doesn't need Hayashida Airi.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.340
As you all know,

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:41.430
I am currently responsible 
for managing Wake Up, Girls!.

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:42.790
Let me cut to the chase.

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:45.150
I'm thinking of cutting 
Hayashida Airi from the group.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:47.410
Hold on! You can't just...

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.000
I just told you.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:51.410
You're currently under my control.

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:55.640
If you're willing to cut 
Hayashida Airi now,

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.420
I will continue your lessons.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:01.420
If you can't, you're all fired.

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:05.420
Give me your decision in ten minutes.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:14.890
To be continued

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.810
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:47.880
Yoppi, what does "thanx" mean?

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:49.280
I think it's a different way 
of saying "thank you".

00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:51.260
What about "fishing it 
up with a girl in Ginza"?

00:23:51.260 --> 00:23:53.160
Minami, where did you 
learn these words?

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:55.760
Maybe I can turn "it's really 
tasty" into "meow, it's tasty for real real"!

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:57.510
I don't think that's 
what it's about...

00:23:57.510 --> 00:24:00.000
The next episode is 
"Wonderful Friends!"

00:23:57.510 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>"Wonderful Friends"</b>
